'''Scarif''' was a remote, tropical [[planet]] located in the [[Abrion sector]] of [[the galaxy]]'s [[Outer Rim Territories]]. Although a small and idyllic world, Scarif played an important part in the [[Galactic Empire]]'s [[Imperial Military|military]]-industrial complex, becoming the center for top-secret research beyond inspection distance of the prying eyes of the [[Imperial Senate]]. Among the projects stored here was the [[DS-1 Orbital Battle Station|Death Star]] [[battle station]], a construction project so important that the entire planet was covered by a [[Planetary shield|planetary]] [[deflector shield]] that could only be entered via the [[Shield Gate]], a [[Golan M3185 space station]].

==Description==
[[File:Acme-ScarifForces.png|thumb|left|300px|The beautiful world of Scarif was turned into a military base for secret projects.]]
Scarif was a verdant,<ref name="VE" /> beautiful if relatively small [[Planet|world]], measuring just over nine thousand [[kilometer]]s in diameter. It had a remote and isolated [[The galaxy|galactic]] location<ref name="UVG" /> in the [[Abrion sector]] of the southeast [[Outer Rim Territories]].<ref name="RO World Locations" /> A deep-[[Color|blue]] world speckled with clouds,<ref name="Rogue One novel" /> Scarif was comprised of tropical, [[Volcano|volcanic]] island chains rising from clear, shallow [[ocean]]s.<ref name="UVG" /> Deeper oceans teeming with life were surrounded by rocky archipelagos.<ref name="Rogue One novel" /> The planet's mantle was filled with dense metals that became valuable in [[starship]] construction. Scarif's sandy beaches were tranquil and idyllic, and some led into jungle canopies filled with wildlife, including [[Areca nut palm tree|areca nut]] [[palm tree]]s and the giant peetalex sea grape, which offered natural protection.<ref name="UVG" /> The world had a [[Temperature|temperate]] and comfortable climate and from the surface appeared as a tropical paradise despite its challenging ecosystem and dangerous [[Diet|predators]].<ref name="VE" />

The [[Galactic Empire]] constructed its [[Imperial Center of Military Research]] across a wheel of islets and landmasses connected by sandy tombolos and artificial transit tubes. The region was surrounded by a volcanic island covered in jungles, and the central islet housed the monolithic [[Citadel Tower]].<ref name="Rogue One novel" /> The Imperial installations on the planet were known to be one of the very few sites where pure, refined [[coaxium]] fuel was stored, other than [[Mercy Island]].<ref name="Solo">''[[Solo: A Star Wars Story]]''</ref>

==History==
===Imperial Era===
{{Quote|Jung.''"<br />"''Sir?''"<br />"''Elaborate on these added protection requests for traffic to the Abrion sector.''"<br />"''Proactive measures, sir. There's an increase in construction shipments going to Scarif, sir.|[[Major]] [[Lio Partagaz]] and [[Lonni Jung]]|<ref name="Aldhani">{{Andor|Aldhani (episode)}}</ref>}}
Although Scarif's planetary mantle was filled with dense metals valuable in [[starship]] construction, its remote location deep within the [[Outer Rim Territories]] meant that supplying [[shipyard]]s of the [[Core Worlds]] proved too costly.<ref name="UVG" /> At one time, a small [[Unidentified Scarif resort|resort]] was based on Scarif, where the [[Scarif Slush]] was served. [[Strono Tuggs]] tried the drink at the resort.<ref name="LDCookbook">''[[Star Wars: The Life Day Cookbook]]''</ref> However, the Galactic Empire saw Scarif as a potential place to house their most classified projects away from the inspection distance of the [[Imperial Senate]]. To this end, the Empire built a major security complex in the planet's northern hemisphere, garrisoned by a special [[Scarif Deployment|deployment]] of the [[Tarkin Initiative]], centered on a Citadel Tower. Large swaths of land were excavated in order to build [[starship]]s, and a high-altitude [[Shield Gate]] station allowed entry past the [[Planetary shield|planetary]] [[deflector shield]],<ref name="UVG" /> which itself was protected by several [[Imperial I-class Star Destroyer|Imperial Star Destroyers]].<ref name="Rogue One" /> Scarif became the principal construction facility for the Empire's vast war machine.<ref name="Scarif DB" />

[[File:RixRoad-DeathStar.png|thumb|right|300px|The Death Star under construction over Scarif]]
Over the years, various officers treated Scarif as a place for an unofficial retirement, where they could neglect their duty in the comfort of a tropical paradise.<ref name="Rogue One novel" /> Codenamed [[Project Stardust]],<ref name="Annual 2">[[Darth Vader Annual 2|''Darth Vader Annual'' 2]]</ref> the designs for an [[armor]]ed [[battle station]] capable of [[Superweapon|destroying]] entire worlds, the [[DS-1 Orbital Battle Station|DS-1 Death Star Mobile Battle Station]], were kept in the massive [[Scarif vault|databanks]] of the Citadel<ref name="Rogue One" /> while the [[battle station]] itself was constructed over the planet [[Geonosis]] under the supervision of [[Director]] [[Orson Callan Krennic]].<ref name="Annual 2" /> Around [[9 BBY]],<ref name="Timelines">''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]''</ref> the Death Star was moved from [[Geonosis]] to Scarif to continue its construction and keep its existence a secret.<ref name="UVG" /> It continued under the supervision of Krennic.<ref name="Rogue One" />

In the final stages of its construction, including the assembly of its [[superlaser]], work on the Death Star was being finished in orbit of Scarif thanks to [[Eta-class supply barge]]s delivering materials, which were then assembled by [[construction droid]]s.<ref name="Rix Road">{{Andor|Rix Road (episode)}}</ref> Despite the importance of the project, the officers of the garrison, commanded by [[General]] [[Sotorus Ramda]], became complacent, mainly because of the confidence placed in Scarif's defenses,<ref name="UVG" /> which included at least two [[Imperial-class Star Destroyer]]s, a [[Cantwell-class Arrestor Cruiser]], as well as many [[TIE/ln space superiority starfighter]]s stored in the hangars of the shield gate.<ref name="Rix Road">{{Andor|Rix Road (episode)}}</ref>

===Galactic Civil War===
{{Main|Battle of Scarif}}
{{Quote|He said we can find the plans. That they're in a data vault on the planet Scarif. Tell the Alliance: they have to go to Scarif and get the plans.|Jyn Erso, to Cassian Jeron Andor on [[Galen Walton Erso|her father's]] message|<ref name="Rogue One novel" />}}
[[File:Battle_of_Scarif_OFL.png|thumb|left|250px|Imperial forces and the forces of Rogue One fought each other on Scarif.]]
The [[Battle of Scarif]] was a battle between the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic|Rebel Alliance]] and the Galactic Empire, taking place in the year [[1 BBY]].<ref name="Timelines" /> The Rebels had received information from [[Jyn Erso]] that the Death Star plans were being [[Scarif vault|held]] in the Citadel Tower, and decided to attempt to capture them. The group successfully infiltrated the tower and successfully managed to transmit the plans to [[Princess]] [[Leia Skywalker Organa Solo|Leia Organa]] and the [[Rebel Alliance Navy|Alliance Fleet]].<ref name="Rogue One" />

As the battle came to its end, [[Grand Moff]] [[Wilhuff Tarkin]] ordered the Death Star to fire a precise single reactor blast at the [[planet]] in an effort to halt the transmission, as well as to eliminate his longtime rival Krennic. The blast did not destroy Scarif itself<ref name="Rogue One" /> but dissipated its planetary shield<ref name="Rogue One novel" /> and obliterated the Citadel Tower, as well as everyone in its vicinity.<ref name="Rogue One" /> The Death Star's superlaser boiled the oceans of Scarif, burning a part of the planet's surface.<ref name="Alphabet Squadron">[[Alphabet Squadron (novel)|''Alphabet Squadron'']]</ref> The Scarif Slush recipe had been smuggled off of Scarif by that point, allowing the drink to survive the destruction of its namesake.<ref name="LDCookbook" />

==Behind the scenes==
Scarif is a tropical planet that was created for the [[2016]] [[Star Wars Anthology Series|''Star Wars'' anthology film]] ''[[Rogue One: A Star Wars Story]]''. The first footage of the planet was shown in the ''Rogue One'' teaser trailer that was released on [[April 7]], [[2016]].<ref name="Teaser">{{SWYouTube|2BDyeARyIkw|Rogue One: A Star Wars Story Trailer Tease}}</ref> The planet's islands were filmed in the Maldives, while the interior of the Citadel Tower was filmed at the Canary Wharf stop on the London Underground.<ref name="UVG" />

Early in ''Rogue One''{{'s}} production, Scarif was conceived as a sort of "dry dock" for the Death Star, with an immense portion of the planet's surface excavated in order to house the battle station.<ref name="Imperial architecture">{{SW|url=news/designing-an-empire-doug-chiang-on-imperial-architecture-in-rogue-one|text=Designing an Empire: Doug Chiang on Imperial Architecture in ''Rogue One''}}</ref>

Director [[Gareth Edwards]] said the planet's nature came about after the crew noticed how [[George Lucas]] had been inspired by every theater of World War II except the Pacific front.<ref>{{WebCite|url=http://legacy.aintitcool.com/node/76862|text=Rogue One's Gareth Edwards discusses, in detail, the creative process behind the very first Star Wars spin-off movie!|author=Vespe, Eric|date=2016-12-05|work=[http://www.aintitcool.com Ain't It Cool News]|archivedate=20190728061448}}</ref>

At the [[2017]] [[Wikipedia:South by Southwest|South by Southwest]] film festival, Edwards revealed that the planet's name, Scarif, came from a misspelling of his name on a coffee cup, telling the audience, "I must have said, 'It's Gareth,' and they wrote 'Scarif.{{' "}}<ref>{{WebCite|url=http://www.hollywoodreporter.com/heat-vision/sxsw-how-a-coffee-cup-mix-up-lead-a-new-star-wars-planet-name-985610|text=SXSW: How a Coffee Cup Mix-Up Led to a New 'Star Wars' Planet Name|author=Natalie Jarvey|date=2017-03-13|work=www.hollywoodreporter.com|archivedate=20170313213733}}</ref>

